WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
What I call bricks without straw features to them

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.000
on bricks Without Straw projects. And I'm sure you've all experienced this. I'd be astounded if you haven't

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.000
So one project that I worked on

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:32.000
It was about 100 people. It was government project. It was kind of automate an ancient process. Kind of turn the whole thing, digitize the whole process.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.000
And

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:50.000
So there was lots and lots of work going on which made it kind of a stretch. It was going to be difficult because it was attempting to digitize this process from beginning to end that had been run on paper for kind of hundreds and hundreds of years. So that was a stretch

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.000
But kind of

00:00:52.000 --> 00:01:02.000
The extra bet that they'd kind of like laid on top of that, amongst others was that this could be done

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.000
With terrible

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:08.000
Internet connections, just like kind of with

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:17.000
appalling connections to the Internet. At one point, one of the people that I was working with when we were trying to raise this problem

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.000
said

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:23.000
In order to make internets, you need internets.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:28.000
kind of having to explain to somebody that that's actually what you need to do.

